  {
    "sha": "8b7c96079f22758ef3b09f2817ea9a06aa5d64b1",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVyylVtoAKDhiN2M5NjA3OWYyMjc1OGVmM2IwOWYyODE3ZWE5YTA2YWE1ZDY0YjE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T17:20:39Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T17:20:39Z"
      },
      "message": "test(post): make the two stale Mach3 conformance goldens again\n\nMain changed the slot and the zigzag pocket generators and made the\ngoldens of the other posts again. The Mach3 goldens of\npocket_zigzag_plate_with_island and slot_wide_channel_rows were the\nold programs, so the conformance test failed on them.\n\nWRITE_GOLDEN=1 on every_builtin_posts_every_golden_byte_exact changed\nonly these two files. The motion (G0/G1/G2/G3, X Y Z I J F) is the\nsame as the grblHAL goldens of the same parts, move for move. It is\nthe same as the Mach4 goldens, except for one extra G0 X Y at the\ncurrent Z of the first-traverse law (no change of position).\n\nRefs #2482\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
