  {
    "sha": "ccfe4199eb8dfe1df3f0c0888a9a4419f4bf40b1",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVyylVtoAKGNjZmU0MTk5ZWI4ZGZlMWRmM2YwYzA4ODhhOWE0NDE5ZjRiZjQwYjE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T17:21:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T17:21:02Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse a G73 or G85 dwell in the Mach3 post by name\n\nThe PECK (G73) and REAM (G85) cycles with a dwell above 0 posted with\nno P word and no message: the dwell was dropped. \"Using Mach3Mill\"\n(release 1.84) gives these formats with no P word:\n10.7.22 \"G73 X~ Y~ Z~ A~ B~ C~ R~ L~ Q~\" and\n10.7.24.6 \"G85 X~ Y~ Z~ A~ B~ C~ R~ L~\". G82, G86 and G89 have P~.\n\nThe script now refuses the dwell by name, in the same form as\ngrblhal.cps (#2609), and writes no cycle block for that hole. Mach3 is\nin the post table of g73_g85_dwell_linuxcnc.rs: mach3_refuses_g73_dwell\nand mach3_refuses_g85_dwell were red before this change and are green\nafter it. A zero dwell posts as before.\n\nRefs #2482\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
