      },
      "message": "fix(post): set axisInversion in the Mach3 post and note a WcsFlip\n\nassets/posts/AGENTS.md says that each built-in mill post sets\naxisInversion = true. The Mach3 script did not, so the engine refused a\nflipped WCS axis or an inverted machine axis by name. The script now\nhas the same form as grblhal.cps and mach4.cps:\n- axisInversion = true in the manifest;\n- the \"MACHINE X+ MOVES LEFT - INVERTED AXIS\" header notes;\n- PARAM WcsFlip read per section, and the\n  \"WCS X FLIPPED - PROGRAM MIRRORED\" note in the preamble, reset at\n  section end.\n\nMach3 is in the table of wcs_flip_dialects.rs (no G41/G42, so\ncomp: false). The trace test reads the mirrored programs back on a\nreversed controller. The new golden golden/wcs_flip/mach3_x.nc locks\nthe X-flipped program. An upright machine posts byte for byte the\nsame: the conformance goldens of Mach3 did not change.\n\nRefs #2482\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
